{"name":"Pink Scallop","hex":"#f2e0d4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"},{"term":"scallop","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various marine bivalve molluscs of the superfamily Pectinoidea.","One of a series of curves, forming an edge similar to a scallop shell, especially in knitting and crochet."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To create or form an edge in the shape of a crescent or multiple crescents.","To bake in a casserole (gratin), originally in a scallop shell; especially used in form scalloped"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scallop"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chlamys rubida","blocks":[{"text":"Chlamys rubida is a species of bivalve mollusc in the family Pectinidae found on the west coast of North America from the Gulf of Alaska to San Diego, California."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Naturalis_Biodiversity_Center_-_ZMA.MOLL.10924_1_-_Chlamys_rubida_%28Hinds%2C_1845%29_-_Pectinidae_-_Mollusc_shell.jpeg/330px-Naturalis_Biodiversity_Center_-_ZMA.MOLL.10924_1_-_Chlamys_rubida_%28Hinds%2C_1845%29_-_Pectinidae_-_Mollusc_shell.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chlamys_rubida","wikidata":"Q3016144"},{"title":"Scallop","blocks":[{"text":"Scallop is a common name that encompasses various species of marine bivalve molluscs in the taxonomic family Pectinidae, the scallops. However, this common name is also sometimes applied to species in other closely related families within the superfamily Pectinoidea, which also includes the thorny oysters."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Argopecten_irradians.jpg/330px-Argopecten_irradians.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scallop","wikidata":"Q1311395"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Opened_scallop_shell.jpg/500px-Opened_scallop_shell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Opened_scallop_shell.jpg/500px-Opened_scallop_shell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A live opened scallop showing the internal anatomy: The pale orange circular part is the adductor muscle; the darker orange curved part is the \"coral\", a culinary term for the ovary or roe.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOpened_scallop_shell.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/74/Fast_and_slow_adductor_muscles_of_the_Yesso_scallop%2C_Patinopecten_yessoensis.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/74/Fast_and_slow_adductor_muscles_of_the_Yesso_scallop%2C_Patinopecten_yessoensis.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Adductor muscles of a scallop. a: photo in a live scallop. b: after remo